{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Let the waters be gathered under the heavens</b> — The tehom, which is water and earth-matter mixed, was like muddy water. He decreed upon the waters that they gather in one place, surrounding all sides, and He decreed upon the earth-matter that it rise until it appears above the water and dries, so that the dry land becomes a level surface suitable for settlement. And thus it is written: \"who spread out the earth upon the waters\" (Psalms 136:6). Or perhaps it [the earth] is spherical, part of it exposed and most of it submerged, as the Greeks imagine by means of their visible proofs or their persuasive arguments. Now these are two decrees, that is, two matters brought about by the will of Elohim contrary to what is natural for them, for given the heaviness of the earth-matter and the lightness of the water opposite it, the natural course would be for the column of the earth to be central and the waters covering it to surround it on every side. Therefore He said \"let the waters be gathered under the heavens,\" that is, to a place of lowness, and He said \"let the dry land appear,\" and He called them names when they assumed these forms, for at first their name was \"tehom.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The word עָפָר here refers to the earthen component mixed within the primordial tehom; rendered \"earth-matter\" to preserve Ramban's technical usage distinguishing it from the formed אֶרֶץ."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:28:53.388387613Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}